  { number := 216, text := "6. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 217, text := "" },
  { number := 218, text := "### 4.10 Sibling line encodings for every published numbered specification" },
  { number := 219, text := "" },
  { number := 220, text := "1. Every published numbered specification markdown `NNNN_descriptive_name.md` at this repository root SHALL have an adjacent Lean spec encoding `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` at the same root (Clause 3.9)." },
  { number := 221, text := "2. Every physical line of that markdown, including blank lines, SHALL have a Lean encoding (line numbers that start at 1, exact text, optional role)." },
  { number := 222, text := "3. Proofs of those encodings SHALL live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, not in `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean`." },
  { number := 223, text := "4. Mixing those encodings with their proofs in one file is a mash that hides the split (Clause 3.5) and is nonconforming in this specifications repository." },
  { number := 224, text := "5. Encoded text SHALL match the file bytes' lines (LF). Authors SHALL NOT wrap encoded lines or change their breaks." },
  { number := 225, text := "6. The Lean program `line_encodings_check` SHALL fail when a markdown line has no encoding or an encoding has no matching markdown line (Clause 3.10)." },
  { number := 226, text := "7. Identity equalities such as line counts MAY use `rfl` in the encoding module. Theorems about the specification SHALL live in the proof module." },
  { number := 227, text := "8. `lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean` remains the meaning encoding of this specification. `0008_Formal_Vibefication.lean` is the line encoding of this markdown file. Those are not the same module." },
  { number := 228, text := "" },
  { number := 229, text := "### 4.11 Named gate" },
  { number := 230, text := "" },
  { number := 231, text := "1. The named gate for this specifications repository remains the gate specified in `0007_CI.md`:" },
  { number := 232, text := "" },
  { number := 233, text := "```text" },
  { number := 234, text := "nix flake check \"path:$PWD\" --print-build-logs" },
  { number := 235, text := "```" },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "2. Lean 4 SHALL be used to surface logical inconsistency in the encodings and in the proofs." },
  { number := 238, text := "" },
  { number := 239, text := "### 4.12 Science cycle (tests are not enough)" },
  { number := 240, text := "" },
  { number := 241, text := "1. Software development is often not scientific." },
  { number := 242, text := "2. Formal Vibefication MUST require, in addition to tests: a hypothesis, a model, a theory, a proof, and corollary experiments so the model is checked against observation of how the system actually behaves." },
  { number := 243, text := "3. Tests SHALL NOT be treated as enough by themselves." },
  { number := 244, text := "4. A fixture that has tests and no model does not conform." },
  { number := 245, text := "5. A fixture that has a model and proofs and no corollary experiments does not conform." },
  { number := 246, text := "6. A fixture that has a hypothesis, a model, a theory, a proof, tests, and corollary experiments does conform for this cycle." },
  { number := 247, text := "7. Companion Lean SHALL treat a fixture that has tests and no model as not conforming, and SHALL treat a fixture that has a model and proofs and no corollary experiments as not conforming. This document does not paste those theorems." },
  { number := 248, text := "" },
  { number := 249, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 250, text := "" },
  { number := 251, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 252, text := "" },
  { number := 253, text := "1. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read and is not treated as a substitute for Lean spec encodings (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 254, text := "2. The specification is encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true, in modules marked as spec encodings rather than proofs (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 255, text := "3. Proofs live in separate Lean modules that import those encodings (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 256, text := "4. `spec_check` remains form of numbered markdown; spec encodings of meaning are not a second markdown form checker (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 257, text := "5. Mixing spec encoding declarations and their proofs in one mash that hides the split is treated as nonconforming for this repository; companion Lean treats that mash as `False` (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 258, text := "6. This specifications repository keeps human markdown, Lean spec encodings, and Lean proofs distinct; Systems Lean product trees may unify specification, proof, and implementation; a mash of those homes is treated as `False` (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 259, text := "7. Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URLs; a numbered specification that names Keagan or Proof of Keags also contains the host `proofofkeags.com`; theorems cover exactly what they state (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 260, text := "8. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are treated as ongoing and not ready for use, and are not described as never started or as ready (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 261, text := "9. fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado remain unspecified; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (`0009_PDOSS.md`) and is not assigned to fargo or Carbonado; Unlicense remains the license; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 262, text := "10. Every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown; proofs of those encodings live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`; a mash of that sibling encoding with its proofs is nonconforming; `line_encodings_check` fails on drift (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 263, text := "11. The named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate for this repository (Clause 4.11)." },
  { number := 264, text := "12. A conforming effort includes a hypothesis, a model, a theory, a proof, tests, and corollary experiments; tests without a model do not conform; a model and proofs without corollary experiments do not conform (Clause 4.12)." },
  { number := 265, text := "" },
  { number := 266, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming Surmount product. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
  { number := 267, text := "" },
  { number := 268, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to." },
  { number := 269, text := "" },
  { number := 270, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 271, text := "" },
  { number := 272, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 273, text := "" },
  { number := 274, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 275, text := "" },
  { number := 276, text := "1. fargo is not specified. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, or 0011 for fargo. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 277, text := "2. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is not specified. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 278, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is this specification. Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (`0009_PDOSS.md`). Number 0010 is Surmount Systems (`0010_Surmount_Systems.md`). Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 279, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 280, text := "5. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) by operator order. Unlicense remains the license. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 281, text := "" },
  { number := 282, text := "### 6.2 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 283, text := "" },
  { number := 284, text := "1. This document specifies Formal Vibefication for this specifications repository. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 285, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md`. This document does not claim that match already holds. The match is not claimed done. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use." },
  { number := 286, text := "3. The SSSSS and beastdb reality check named in `0007_CI.md` is a requirement on that stack. SSSSS and beastdb are ongoing and not ready for use. Do not write that they never started or do not exist. This document does not claim the check is done." },
  { number := 287, text := "4. `lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean` encodes selected claims, including the science cycle (hypothesis, model, theory, proof, tests, and corollary experiments). `lean/FormalVibeficationProofs.lean` proves those claims. `lean/Surmount.lean` composes stack identities. `0008_Formal_Vibefication.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0008.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that Slake emit already matches `ELF`. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use." },
  { number := 288, text := "" },
  { number := 289, text := "### 6.3 Companion meaning models split encodings and proofs" },
  { number := 290, text := "" },
  { number := 291, text := "1. This specification requires the split in Clause 4.2 and Clause 4.3 for spec encodings and proofs in this repository." },
  { number := 292, text := "2. Companion models for CATE (`lean/CateSpec.lean` encodings, `lean/CateProofs.lean` theorems), RSI (`lean/RsiSpec.lean`, `lean/RsiProofs.lean`), Continuous Integration (`lean/CiSpec.lean`, `lean/CiProofs.lean`), beastdb (encodings and proofs under `lean/` for that product), SSSSS (`lean/SssssSpec.lean`, `lean/SssssProofs.lean`), Systems Lean (`lean/SystemsLeanSpec.lean`, `lean/SystemsLeanProofs.lean`), Formal Vibefication (`lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean`, `lean/FormalVibeficationProofs.lean`), Unlicense (`lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean`, `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean`), Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`lean/TechTreeSpec.lean`, `lean/TechTreeProofs.lean`), Majestic Memex (`lean/MemexSpec.lean`, `lean/MemexProofs.lean`), Lean Machine (`lean/LeanMachineSpec.lean`, `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`), and the CATE word catalog (`lean/VocabularySpec.lean`, `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`) place encodings in Spec modules and theorems in Proofs modules. Collision tags in `lean/Vocabulary.lean` are encodings with proofs in `lean/VocabularyCollisionProofs.lean`. Mixing encodings and proofs in one mash is `False`. It is not a claim that those products never started." },
  { number := 293, text := "3. That split is present for the companion meaning models named in item 2." },
  { number := 294, text := "4. Sibling line encodings `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` and proof modules `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean` exist for every published numbered markdown file. That split is not a claim that products are ready for use." },
  { number := 295, text := "" },
  { number := 296, text := "### 6.4 Pins this document does not add" },
  { number := 297, text := "" },
  { number := 298, text := "1. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are not pins of this specifications repository's `ref/`. `0002_Systems_Lean.md` places those Form 1 pins in the Systems Lean product tree. This repository MUST NOT copy those four trees into this repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 299, text := "2. Formal Vibefication essays are cited by URL. They are not Clause 12 pins. This repository does not vendor those essays as Form 2 copies under `ref/`. Full license text is still not published on https://proofofkeags.com . Do not invent that license." },
  { number := 300, text := "3. ISO 24495-1:2023 and the US Federal Plain Language Guidelines remain informative prior art of CATE. They are not pins of this document." },
