  { number := 311, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 312, text := "" },
  { number := 313, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260831" },
  { number := 314, text := "" },
  { number := 315, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Changelog history records that a 1.0.0 line existed. This line also records the science cycle: Formal Vibefication requires a hypothesis, a model, a theory, a proof, tests, and corollary experiments; tests alone are not enough." },
  { number := 316, text := "" },
  { number := 317, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 318, text := "" },
  { number := 319, text := "First publication of Formal Vibefication as numbered specification 0008 with file name `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. Records that numbered markdown is the contract humans read and is not a substitute for Lean spec encodings. Requires the specification to be encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true, in modules marked as spec encodings. Requires proofs to live in separate Lean modules that import those encodings. Records that Lean proofs are not the specification. Records that `spec_check` is form of numbered markdown and is not a second meaning linter. Treats a mash of spec encodings and their proofs that hides the split as nonconforming in this specifications repository. Records that Systems Lean product trees may unify specification, proof, and implementation, and that mashing that home with this repository's split is `False`. Cites Formal Vibefication and Taking Don't Trust. Verify. Seriously with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and requires back linking. Requires residual honesty that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are ongoing and not ready for use." },
  { number := 320, text := "" },
  { number := 321, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; Continuous Integration is specification 0007; Surmount Systems is specification 0010; this specification is number 0008; number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (`0009_PDOSS.md`) and the word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`); a numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP is not specified; Carbonado has no assigned number; Lean Machine is specified as `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; companion meaning models named in Clause 6.3 split encodings from proofs and treat mash as False; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown, with proofs in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, checked by `line_encodings_check`; this document does not claim that a conforming Surmount product exists." },
